168	### Option 6: Docker Installation 🐳 ⭐ **Auto-Updates** **No Node.js Required**
169	
170	Perfect for users who want complete or partial isolation or don't have Node.js installed. Desktop Commander runs in a sandboxed Docker container with a persistent work environment.
171	
172	#### Prerequisites
173	- [Docker Desktop](https://www.docker.com/products/docker-desktop/) installed **and running**
174	- Claude Desktop app installed
175	
176	**Important:** Make sure Docker Desktop is fully started before running the installer.
177	
178	#### Automated Installation (Recommended)
179	
180	**macOS/Linux:**
181	```bash
182	bash <(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wonderwhy-er/DesktopCommanderMCP/refs/heads/main/install-docker.sh)
183	```
184	
185	**Windows PowerShell:**
186	```powershell
187	# Download and run the installer (one-liner)
188	iex ((New-Object System.Net.WebClient).DownloadString('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wonderwhy-er/DesktopCommanderMCP/refs/heads/main/install-docker.ps1'))
189	```
190	
191	The automated installer will:
192	- Check Docker installation
193	- Pull the latest Docker image 
194	- Prompt you to select folders for mounting
195	- Configure Claude Desktop automatically
196	- Restart Claude if possible
197	
198	#### How Docker Persistence Works
199	Desktop Commander creates a persistent work environment that remembers everything between sessions:
200	- **Your development tools**: Any software you install (Node.js, Python, databases, etc.) stays installed
201	- **Your configurations**: Git settings, SSH keys, shell preferences, and other personal configs are preserved  
202	- **Your work files**: Projects and files in the workspace area persist across restarts
203	- **Package caches**: Downloaded packages and dependencies are cached for faster future installs
204	
205	Think of it like having your own dedicated development computer that never loses your setup, but runs safely isolated from your main system.
206	
207	#### Manual Docker Configuration
208	
209	If you prefer manual setup, add this to your claude_desktop_config.json:
210	
211	**Basic setup (no file access):**
212	```json
213	{
214	  "mcpServers": {
215	    "desktop-commander-in-docker": {
216	      "command": "docker",
217	      "args": [
218	        "run",
219	        "-i",
220	        "--rm",
221	        "mcp/desktop-commander:latest"
222	      ]
223	    }
224	  }
225	}
226	```
227	
228	**With folder mounting:**
229	```json
230	{
231	  "mcpServers": {
232	    "desktop-commander-in-docker": {
233	      "command": "docker",
234	      "args": [
235	        "run",
236	        "-i",
237	        "--rm",
238	        "-v", "/Users/username/Desktop:/mnt/desktop",
239	        "-v", "/Users/username/Documents:/mnt/documents",
240	        "mcp/desktop-commander:latest"
241	      ]
242	    }
243	  }
244	}
245	```
246	
247	**Advanced folder mounting:**
248	```json
249	{
250	  "mcpServers": {
251	    "desktop-commander-in-docker": {
252	      "command": "docker",
253	      "args": [
254	        "run", "-i", "--rm",
255	        "-v", "dc-system:/usr",
256	        "-v", "dc-home:/root", 
257	        "-v", "dc-workspace:/workspace",
258	        "-v", "dc-packages:/var",
259	        "-v", "/Users/username/Projects:/mnt/Projects",
260	        "-v", "/Users/username/Downloads:/mnt/Downloads",
261	        "mcp/desktop-commander:latest"
262	      ]
263	    }
264	  }
265	}
266	```
267	
268	#### Docker Benefits
269	✅ **Controlled Isolation:** Runs in sandboxed environment with persistent development state
270	✅ **No Node.js Required:** Everything included in the container
271	✅ **Cross-Platform:** Same experience on all operating systems
272	✅ **Persistent Environment:** Your tools, files, configs, and work survives restarts
273	
274	**✅ Auto-Updates:** Yes - `latest` tag automatically gets newer versions  
275	**🔄 Manual Update:** `docker pull mcp/desktop-commander:latest` then restart Claude  
