200	## Troubleshooting
201	
202	### Issue 1: MCP Server Not Showing Up
203	**Symptoms**: Không thấy 🔌 icon hoặc tools không available
204	
205	**Solutions**:
206	1. Check config file syntax (valid JSON)
207	2. Check paths (absolute paths, double backslashes)
208	3. Check .env file exists with OPENPROJECT_URL and OPENPROJECT_API_KEY
209	4. Restart Claude Code completely
210	
211	**Verify manually**:
212	```bash
213	cd d:\Promete\Project\mcp-openproject\openproject-mcp-server
214	uv run python openproject-mcp-fastmcp.py
215	# Should see: "Loading tool modules..." and "Tool modules loaded successfully"
216	```
217	
218	---
219	
220	### Issue 2: Connection Failed
221	**Symptoms**: "❌ Connection failed" error
222	
223	**Solutions**:
224	1. Check `.env` file:
225	```env
226	OPENPROJECT_URL=https://manage.promete.ai
227	OPENPROJECT_API_KEY=your_actual_api_key_here
228	```
229	
230	2. Test connection manually:
231	```bash
232	uv run python test_tools.py
233	```
234	
235	3. Check OpenProject is accessible:
236	```bash
237	curl https://manage.promete.ai/api/v3
238	```
239	
240	---
241	
242	### Issue 3: Tools Not Working
243	**Symptoms**: Tools show up but give errors when called
244	
245	**Solutions**:
246	1. Check logs in Claude Code (View → Developer Tools → Console)
247	2. Test individual tool:
248	```bash
249	cd d:\Promete\Project\mcp-openproject\openproject-mcp-server
250	uv run python -c "from src.tools.connection import test_connection; import asyncio; print(asyncio.run(test_connection()))"
251	```
252	
253	---
254	
255	## Advanced: Test HTTP Transport
256	
257	If you want to test HTTP transport for 12 users:
258	
259	### Start HTTP Server
260	```bash
261	cd d:\Promete\Project\mcp-openproject\openproject-mcp-server
262	
263	# Set API keys
264	set MCP_API_KEYS=test-key:TestUser
265	
